    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76-a1">

                <pb facs="0262" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg178"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    81.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Reatrepo to Mr. King.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Columbia, Ministry Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 20, 1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It is as much my pleasure as it is my duty
                    to express to you the gratitude of my Government for the important service which
                    you have rendered to it by contributing in a most essential degree, together
                    with Mr. Arthur Malo O’Leary, to the translation of the national constitution
                    into English.</p>
                <p>Your work will greatly contribute to facilitate the relations between this
                    Republic and the civilized nations which speak that language.</p>
                <p>I renew, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>VICENTE RESTREPO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
